---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../config/site";

const title = "YouTube Analytics Tool Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "Privacy policy for the personal YouTube Analytics tool: what data it accesses, how it is used, and how to revoke access.";
const lastUpdated = "2026-09-11";
const linkClass =
  "underline decoration-zinc-600 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-100 hover:decoration-zinc-300";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-400">
        Privacy Policy
      </p>
      <h1
        class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
        data-ball-obstacle="text"
      >
        YouTube Analytics Tool Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">
        Last updated: <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdated}</time>
      </p>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        This policy describes how the
        <a href="/youtube-analytics/" class={linkClass}
          >YouTube Analytics Tool</a
        >
        ("the tool") handles data. The tool is a private, single-user application
        operated by {siteConfig.name} (Ömer Zeyveli) to read analytics data from my
        own YouTube channel.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        Use of YouTube API Services
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        The tool uses YouTube API Services. By using it, I agree to be bound by
        the
        <a
          href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms"
          class={linkClass}
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">YouTube Terms of Service</a
        >. Data obtained through YouTube API Services is also subject to the
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          class={linkClass}
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Data accessed</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        After I sign in with my Google account and grant permission, the tool
        requests read-only access to the following data for the YouTube channel
        I own:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        <li>
          Channel analytics reports, such as views, watch time, estimated
          minutes watched, subscriber changes, and traffic sources.
        </li>
        <li>
          Basic channel and video metadata needed to label those reports, such
          as channel name, video titles, and video IDs.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        The tool does not request write access. It cannot upload, edit, or
        delete videos, comments, playlists, or channel settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How data is used</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        <li>Data is used only to display analytics reports to me.</li>
        <li>
          Data is not sold, shared with third parties, or used for advertising.
        </li>
        <li>
          Data is not used to build profiles of any person other than the
          channel owner, and no other users exist.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        Storage and retention
      </h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        <li>
          OAuth tokens are stored locally on my own device so that I do not have
          to sign in every time. They are never transmitted anywhere other than
          to Google's APIs.
        </li>
        <li>
          Fetched analytics data may be cached locally for convenience. Cached
          data is deleted when I clear it or remove the tool.
        </li>
        <li>
          No data is stored on a server operated by me, and this website does
          not collect or store any data from the tool.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        The tool itself does not set cookies or use analytics or tracking
        services. Google may set cookies during the Google sign-in flow, which
        is governed by the Google Privacy Policy linked above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Revoking access</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        Access granted to the tool can be revoked at any time from the
        <a
          href="https://security.google.com/settings/security/permissions"
          class={linkClass}
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Google security settings page</a
        >. Revoking access immediately invalidates the stored OAuth tokens. Any
        locally cached data can be removed by deleting the tool's local files.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        This policy may be updated if the tool's behaviour changes. The date at
        the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 text-zinc-300">
        Questions about this policy can be sent through
        <a
          href={siteConfig.social.github}
          class={linkClass}
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">GitHub</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
